# Never run `npm run build` while `npm run dev` is running

Both write to `.next/`. A production build replaces `.next/static` with hashed
production chunks, so the running dev server 404s on its own assets:

```
GET /_next/static/chunks/main-app.js            404
GET /_next/static/chunks/app-pages-internals.js 404
GET /_next/static/css/app/layout.css            404
```

Stop the dev server first, or accept that you must clean up afterwards.

# Check for an orphan dev server before starting one

They survive for days and silently push the new server onto port 3001+, and two
`next dev` processes sharing `.next/cache/webpack` corrupt it. Symptoms are
`ENOENT: rename '0.pack.gz_' -> '0.pack.gz'` and
`SyntaxError: Unexpected non-whitespace character after JSON at position 4`.

```powershell
Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 3000 -State Listen -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |
  ForEach-Object { Get-CimInstance Win32_Process -Filter "ProcessId=$($_.OwningProcess)" |
    Select-Object ProcessId, CommandLine }
```

Recovery: stop every `next dev` for this repo, `Remove-Item -Recurse -Force .next`,
then `npm run dev`.

# Lint has a known baseline

`npm run lint` runs `eslint .`, which walks the committed `.netlify` build output
and reports unresolvable-rule errors there. Lint source only:

```powershell
npx eslint app components lib scripts
```

That still reports 3 pre-existing errors — `app/page.tsx` (`set-state-in-effect`)
and two in `components/TaskModals.tsx` (`refs` during render). Leave them alone
unless asked; just do not add new ones.

# PowerShell, not bash

- No heredocs. For a multi-line commit message, write a file and `git commit -F`.
- `$PID` is read-only; name loop variables something else (`$procId`).
